            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0532" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/25145</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 26.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4171</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that Count
                    Montgelas, the German Minister Designate, called at the Foreign Office this
                    morning to arrange for the presentation of his credentials. Count Montgelas
                    stated to one of my colleagues that after having heard that a new Spanish
                    Minister was <hi rendition="#italic">en route</hi> to this post he so advised
                    his Government and requested, if this report could be confirmed at Madrid, that
                    he be instructed to recognize the Obregon Government.</p>
                <p>I regret that the Embassy’s contingent allotment is not sufficiently large to
                    permit the above information to be telegraphed.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George T.
                    Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
